<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.21424v1/sensitivity_3panel.svg" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/160;" width="548" height="160"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A2.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Sensitivity to Prior Skew.<span id="A2.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (Left) Functional degradation on the rare mode most pronounced at <math id="A2.F5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.98</annotation></semantics></math>. (Center) Behavioural distance <math id="A2.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> decreasing as skew increases. (Right) Decay of internal representation geometry across biased priors, preceding functional failure.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Effect of Network Capacity under Extreme Skew</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test whether erosion is an artifact of limited architectural capacity, we swept the hidden dimension <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\{32,64,128\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\{32,64,128\}</annotation></semantics></math> under a fixed extreme bias (<math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.98</annotation></semantics></math>). Final values are summarized in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.4 Effect of Network Capacity under Extreme Skew ‣ Appendix B Supplemental Material: Experimental Details ‣ On the Structural Non-Preservation of Epistemic Behaviour under Policy Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Increasing recurrent capacity does not prevent behavioural erosion under extreme skew. While the <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=128</annotation></semantics></math> model begins with a larger initial representational separation, it exhibits greater variability during training compared to smaller models (Figure <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ B.4 Effect of Network Capacity under Extreme Skew ‣ Appendix B Supplemental Material: Experimental Details ‣ On the Structural Non-Preservation of Epistemic Behaviour under Policy Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Final Epistemic Metrics by Network Capacity (<math id="A2.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>) at <math id="A2.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.98</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mean\pm se" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mean\pm se</annotation></semantics></math>, 10 seeds)</span></figcaption>
